Steve Look <slook@mchsi.com> wrote:
> I finally have {I think anyway} RH7.2 installed on my 4/233. Now the issue
> is to boot it. I have read the various guides but still do not have much of
> a clue as to how to boot. Much of the material references sites that don't
> exist anymore. Can somebody provide an easy guide to set up a boot disk? I
> understand it involves MILO and linload,

No, it does not if you are not using ARC console (and if you really
do not _have to_ use it then forget about it).

> I have both SRM and ARC consoles.

See above.

What is your boot device? 'sh dev' at SRM prompt will help you
to identify that.  Assuming that you were not using a recycled disk
with an unerased old "FAT style" partition table on which to install,
and that this disk is, say, dka100 for SRM then type

  b dka100 -fl 0

at SRM prompt and it should boot.

If you will set 'bootdef_dev' to 'dka100' and 'boot_osflags' to 0
then you can just type 'b' and this will boot.  Once you have everything
correct then you can set 'auto_action' to BOOT and this will boot
automagically on a power up.  Things are defined in your 'aboot.conf'
file.

There are documentes, like 'SRM HOWTO' on http://www.alphalinux.org/
Also type at SRM prompt things like
help | more
show * | more
and other things in that style to find out more.

Looking (on Google, say) through archives of this newsgroup would
also reveal such mysteries of a universe.  In particular what to
do if you had that old partition table (in short - erase it and
reinstall).

When in action immediately retrieve and install updates.  There is
a lot of these.

   Michal


