With NT the minimum recommended mem is 64mb even though the requirement is a
min. of 32mb.  Trust me with 32mb ram you will pretty much be confined to
running 1 program at a time. 128mb of ram is even better, you can load the
kernel into memory and most of your drivers and even a few proggies...

As for video? Hmmm, go with something like a Matrox G500 or G450... Its the
fastest ALPHA compatible PCI video card around that doesn't cost a small
fortune. It's also supported by Directx 9.x for a maximum speed boost
without the 'normal' cpu load. The reason I recommend a Matrox is because
the Matrox has on onboard chip that makes the card detectable by most if not
all Alphas. Other cards such as NVidia are often not usable.

If you want to increase your IDE speed, well all I can say is, "Alpha IDE
supports SUCKS... It's either SCSI or nothing."


