noticed SIGNIFICANT speed increases especially in the area of I/O =
related programs such as initialization of KDE and GNOME. My compile =
times for software were literally cut in half. The only problem? At load =
the kernel would generate error messages and isn't fully optimized for =
the PCA56 but the EV5, no multimedia extensions and the like such as =
MVI.

We need to email petition Kernel.org and ask that they recognize the =
AlphaPC 164SX as being a separate and POPULAR format. If they can =
support the EB164 and EB64+, why can't they support the AlphaPC 164SX =
which is more advanced and FASTER than both the AlphaPC 164 and the =
164SX (also both supported)?=20

Please direct your emails to:linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org  and please =
remember to be nice and polite, these guys work for free!
