At least if the vectors are the same on your hardware as on
a UP2000, this machine check vector indicates a serious
hardware problem.  Vector 0x630 is a correctable ECC error.
At the time I was first seeing those, I was told vector
0x630 was correctable and 0x670 was an uncorrectable ECC
error.  I would suggest testing your RAM using SRM and/or
substitution.

Regarding the other responses about Gnome being bloated, it
may be Gnome's memory footprint and access pattern tickles
the bad memory location while KDE does not.

